{"task_id": "Mbpp/7", "solution": "def find_char_long(input_string: str) -> list[str]:\n    \"\"\"Extracts words of at least 4 characters from an input string.\n    Words are identified by splitting whitespace and stripping common punctuation.\"\"\"\n\n    # Define common punctuation characters to strip from word ends.\n    # This list is defined inline to avoid importing modules like 'string'.\n    punctuation_chars = '.,!?;:\"\\'()-[]{}/\\\\`~@#$%^&*+='\n\n    words = input_string.split()\n    long_words = []\n\n    for word in words:\n        # Strip leading and trailing punctuation from the word.\n        cleaned_word = word.strip(punctuation_chars)\n\n        # Check if the cleaned word has at least 4 characters.\n        if len(cleaned_word) >= 4:\n            long_words.append(cleaned_word)\n\n    return long_words"}
