{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "def is_samepatterns(array1, array2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if two arrays follow the same structural pattern, requiring a one-to-one mapping\n    between their unique elements while preserving sequence.\n    Arrays must have the same length for a pattern match to be possible.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(array1) != len(array2):\n        return False\n\n    map1_to_2 = {}\n    map2_to_1 = {}\n\n    for i in range(len(array1)):\n        element1 = array1[i]\n        element2 = array2[i]\n\n        # Check existing mappings for consistency (AF2 from design)\n        if element1 in map1_to_2:\n            if map1_to_2[element1] != element2:\n                return False\n        if element2 in map2_to_1:\n            if map2_to_1[element2] != element1:\n                return False\n\n        # Check for conflicting new mappings (AF3 from design)\n        # This covers cases where one element is new, but its counterpart is already mapped.\n        if (element1 not in map1_to_2) and (element2 in map2_to_1):\n            return False\n        if (element2 not in map2_to_1) and (element1 in map1_to_2):\n            return False\n\n        # Establish or update mappings if no conflicts found\n        map1_to_2[element1] = element2\n        map2_to_1[element2] = element1\n\n    return True"}
