{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "def is_samepatterns(strings: list, patterns: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a list of strings follows a pattern sequence, ensuring consistent one-to-one mapping.\n    Returns True if mapping holds consistently, False otherwise (e.g., unequal lengths, inconsistencies).\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(strings) != len(patterns):\n        return False\n\n    pattern_to_string_map = {}\n    string_to_pattern_map = {}\n\n    for i in range(len(strings)):\n        current_string = strings[i]\n        current_pattern = patterns[i]\n\n        # Check pattern_to_string_map consistency\n        if current_pattern in pattern_to_string_map:\n            if pattern_to_string_map[current_pattern] != current_string:\n                return False\n        else:\n            # If pattern is new, check string_to_pattern_map for inverse consistency\n            if current_string in string_to_pattern_map:\n                if string_to_pattern_map[current_string] != current_pattern:\n                    return False\n\n        # Check string_to_pattern_map consistency\n        if current_string in string_to_pattern_map:\n            if string_to_pattern_map[current_string] != current_pattern:\n                return False\n        else:\n            # If string is new, check pattern_to_string_map for inverse consistency\n            if current_pattern in pattern_to_string_map:\n                if pattern_to_string_map[current_pattern] != current_string:\n                    return False\n\n        # Add/Update new mappings if consistent\n        pattern_to_string_map[current_pattern] = current_string\n        string_to_pattern_map[current_string] = current_pattern\n\n    return True"}
