{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "from typing import Dict\n_cache: Dict[int, int] = {}\ndef sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Newman-Conway sequence number.\n    It uses memoization to efficiently compute terms.\n    \"\"\"\n    # CRITICAL REQUIREMENT: Do NOT raise exceptions for edge cases.\n    # Assuming n will always be a positive integer (n >= 1) as per the problem definition.\n\n    if n in _cache:\n        return _cache[n]\n\n    if n == 1 or n == 2:\n        result = 1\n    else:\n        # P(n) = P(P(n - 1)) + P(n - P(n - 1))\n        p_n_minus_1 = sequence(n - 1)\n        result = sequence(p_n_minus_1) + sequence(n - p_n_minus_1)\n\n    _cache[n] = result\n    return result"}
