{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "def sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence.\n\n    The Newman-Conway sequence is defined as:\n    p(1) = 1\n    p(2) = 1\n    p(n) = p(p(n - 1)) + p(n - p(n - 1)) for n > 2\n\n    Args:\n        n: The position in the sequence (a positive integer).\n\n    Returns:\n        The nth number in the Newman-Conway sequence.\n\n    Raises:\n        ValueError: If n is not a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input 'n' must be a positive integer.\")\n\n    memo = {1: 1, 2: 1}\n\n    def _calculate(k: int) -> int:\n        if k in memo:\n            return memo[k]\n\n        # According to the Newman-Conway definition, k should always be > 0\n        # for valid sequence numbers. If an intermediate calculation results\n        # in k <= 0, it indicates an issue or an edge case not covered by typical sequence behavior.\n        if k <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Invalid intermediate value encountered in Newman-Conway sequence calculation.\")\n\n        p_k_minus_1_val = _calculate(k - 1)\n        term1 = _calculate(p_k_minus_1_val)\n        term2 = _calculate(k - p_k_minus_1_val)\n\n        result = term1 + term2\n\n        memo[k] = result\n        return result\n\n    return _calculate(n)"}
