{"task_id": "Mbpp/98", "solution": "def multiply_num(numbers: tuple[float, ...]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the product of all numbers in a list and divides it by the list's length.\n    It ensures floating-point precision throughout the calculation.\"\"\"\n    product = 1.0\n    for number in numbers:\n        product *= number\n\n    count = len(numbers)\n    result = product / count\n\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/99", "solution": "def decimal_to_binary(num):\n    \"\"\"Converts a non-negative decimal integer to its binary string representation.\n    Returns \"0\" for input 0, otherwise no leading zeros.\"\"\"\n    if num == 0:\n        return \"0\"\n\n    binary_digits = []\n    while num > 0:\n        remainder = num % 2\n        binary_digits.append(str(remainder))\n        num //= 2\n\n    return \"\".join(binary_digits[::-1])"}
