{"task_id": "Mbpp/113", "solution": "def check_integer(input_string):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a string represents a valid integer.\n    Handles positive, negative, and zero values, rejecting non-digits, decimals, and whitespace.\n    \"\"\"\n    # 1. Empty String Check: If the input string is empty, it's not a valid integer.\n    if not input_string:\n        return False\n\n    # 2. Whitespace Check: If the string has leading or trailing whitespace, it's invalid.\n    if input_string != input_string.strip():\n        return False\n\n    # 3. Decimal Point Check: If a decimal point is present, it's not an integer.\n    if '.' in input_string:\n        return False\n\n    # 4. Sign and Digit Check:\n    if input_string.startswith('-'):\n        # For negative numbers, the substring after '-' must consist entirely of digits and not be empty.\n        if not input_string[1:]:  # Handles cases like just \"-\"\n            return False\n        return input_string[1:].isdigit()\n    else:\n        # For positive numbers or zero, the entire string must consist entirely of digits.\n        return input_string.isdigit()"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/116", "solution": "def tuple_to_int(input_tuple: tuple) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Converts a tuple of positive integers into a single integer by concatenation.\n\n    An empty tuple returns 0.\n    Raises TypeError if input_tuple is not a tuple or contains non-integer elements.\n    Raises ValueError if input_tuple contains non-positive integer elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(input_tuple, tuple):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a tuple\")\n\n    if not input_tuple:\n        return 0\n\n    string_elements = []\n    for element in input_tuple:\n        if not isinstance(element, int):\n            raise TypeError(\"Tuple elements must be integers\")\n        if element <= 0:\n            raise ValueError(\"Tuple elements must be positive integers\")\n        string_elements.append(str(element))\n\n    concatenated_string = \"\".join(string_elements)\n    return int(concatenated_string)"}
