{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "def sum_proper_divisors(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of proper divisors for a given positive integer n.\n    This excludes n itself.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n\n    total_div_sum = 1  # 1 is always a proper divisor for n > 1\n    # Check divisors up to the square root of n\n    for d in range(2, int(n**0.5) + 1):\n        if n % d == 0:\n            total_div_sum += d\n            if d * d != n:  # If d is not the square root, add its pair\n                total_div_sum += n // d\n    return total_div_sum\ndef amicable_numbers_sum(limit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all amicable numbers from 1 up to the specified limit.\n    This identifies amicable pairs (i, j) where i < j.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for i in range(1, limit):\n        j = sum_proper_divisors(i)\n        # Check if j is a potential amicable partner within the limit and not equal to i\n        if j > 0 and j <= limit and i != j:\n            k = sum_proper_divisors(j)\n            # If k equals i and i is less than j (to avoid double counting pairs)\n            if k == i and i < j:\n                total_sum += i\n                total_sum += j\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/123", "solution": "import math\ndef _sum_proper_divisors(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of positive divisors of n excluding n itself.\n    Optimizes by checking divisors up to sqrt(n).\"\"\"\n    if n == 1:\n        return 0\n    s = 1\n    for i in range(2, int(math.sqrt(n)) + 1):\n        if n % i == 0:\n            s += i\n            if i * i != n:\n                s += n // i\n    return s\ndef amicable_numbers_sum(limit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all amicable numbers up to the specified limit.\n    It identifies amicable pairs (a, b) where sum_proper_divisors(a) = b and sum_proper_divisors(b) = a, with a != b.\"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    found_amicable_numbers = set()\n\n    for num in range(1, limit + 1):\n        if num in found_amicable_numbers:\n            continue\n\n        d_num = _sum_proper_divisors(num)\n\n        # Ensure d_num is a valid candidate for an amicable pair.\n        if d_num > num and d_num <= limit and d_num not in found_amicable_numbers:\n            d_d_num = _sum_proper_divisors(d_num)\n\n            if d_d_num == num:\n                # Found an amicable pair (num, d_num).\n                total_sum += num\n                total_sum += d_num\n                found_amicable_numbers.add(num)\n                found_amicable_numbers.add(d_num)\n\n    return total_sum"}
