{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "def find_length(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum difference between the number of 0s and 1s in any substring.\n    This is achieved by transforming the string and applying Kadane's algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not s:\n        return 0\n\n    transformed_array = []\n    for char in s:\n        if char == '0':\n            transformed_array.append(1)\n        else:  # char == '1'\n            transformed_array.append(-1)\n\n    max_so_far = 0\n    current_max = 0\n    for num in transformed_array:\n        current_max += num\n        if current_max < 0:\n            current_max = 0\n        if current_max > max_so_far:\n            max_so_far = current_max\n\n    return max_so_far"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "def sum_of_common_divisors(a: int, b: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of all common divisors for two positive integers.\n    The function assumes `a` and `b` are positive integers as per critical requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    # Iterate from 1 up to the minimum of a and b (inclusive).\n    # This range covers all possible common divisors for a and b.\n    limit = min(a, b)\n    for i in range(1, limit + 1):\n        if a % i == 0 and b % i == 0:\n            total_sum += i\n    return total_sum"}
