{"task_id": "Mbpp/125", "solution": "def find_length(binary_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum difference between the count of '0's and '1's in any substring.\n    Applies a Kadane's algorithm variant after transforming '0's to 1 and '1's to -1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not binary_string:\n        return 0\n\n    max_diff = 0\n    current_diff = 0\n\n    for char in binary_string:\n        # Transform '0' to 1 and '1' to -1 to find max subarray sum.\n        transformed_value = 1 if char == '0' else -1\n\n        current_diff += transformed_value\n        max_diff = max(max_diff, current_diff)\n\n        # If current sum becomes negative, reset it to 0 as it contributes negatively.\n        if current_diff < 0:\n            current_diff = 0\n\n    return max_diff"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/126", "solution": "def _get_positive_divisors(number: int) -> set[int]:\n    # Returns a set of positive divisors for a given integer.\n    # Special handling for 0 returns an empty set.\n    if number == 0:\n        return set()\n    divisors = set()\n    abs_number = abs(number)\n    for i in range(1, abs_number + 1):\n        if abs_number % i == 0:\n            divisors.add(i)\n    return divisors\n\ndef sum_common_divisors(number1: int, number2: int) -> int:\n    # Calculates the sum of all positive common divisors for two integers.\n    # It finds divisors for each number and then sums their intersection.\n    divisors1 = _get_positive_divisors(number1)\n    divisors2 = _get_positive_divisors(number2)\n    common_divisors = divisors1.intersection(divisors2)\n    return sum(common_divisors)"}
