{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "def zero_count(numbers: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the ratio of zero elements to non-zero elements in an array of integers.\n    Returns 0.0 if there are no non-zero elements.\"\"\"\n    zero_count = 0\n    non_zero_count = 0\n\n    for number in numbers:\n        if number == 0:\n            zero_count += 1\n        else:\n            non_zero_count += 1\n\n    if non_zero_count == 0:\n        return 0.0\n    else:\n        # Perform float division and ensure the result is a float.\n        return float(zero_count) / non_zero_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "def zero_count(array_of_integers: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the ratio of zero elements to non-zero elements in an array of integers.\n    Returns 0.0 if there are no non-zero elements to avoid division by zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    zero_count_val = 0\n    non_zero_count_val = 0\n\n    for element in array_of_integers:\n        if element == 0:\n            zero_count_val += 1\n        else:\n            non_zero_count_val += 1\n\n    if non_zero_count_val == 0:\n        return 0.0\n    else:\n        return float(zero_count_val) / non_zero_count_val"}
