{"task_id": "Mbpp/138", "solution": "def is_Sum_Of_Powers_Of_Two(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a positive integer is a sum of distinct powers of 2 (n >= 1).\n    This means the number must be even, as 2^0 (which is 1) is excluded.\n    \"\"\"\n    # BR2: The input number for the check must be a positive integer.\n    # BR4: The function shall return false if the input number is not a positive integer.\n    if not isinstance(number, int) or number <= 0:\n        return False\n\n    # BR1: A 'non-zero power of 2' refers to 2^n where n is a positive integer (n >= 1).\n    # This means powers like 2, 4, 8, 16, etc., are considered, but 2^0 (which is 1) is not.\n    # If a number is a sum of distinct powers of 2, and none of them is 2^0 (which is 1),\n    # then the number must be even. An odd positive number always includes 2^0 (1) in its\n    # binary representation (sum of distinct powers of 2).\n    # BR3: The function shall return true if the input number can be expressed as a sum of one or more distinct non-zero powers of 2.\n    # BR4: The function shall return false if it cannot be expressed as a sum of distinct non-zero powers of 2.\n    return number % 2 == 0"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/141", "solution": "from typing import List, Any\ndef pancake_sort(arr: List[Any]) -> List[Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sorts a list of elements using the pancake sort algorithm.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Create a copy to avoid modifying the original list in-place\n    elements = list(arr)\n    n = len(elements)\n\n    def _flip(array: List[Any], k: int) -> None:\n        \"\"\"Reverses elements from index 0 to k-1 in the list.\"\"\"\n        start = 0\n        end = k - 1\n        while start < end:\n            array[start], array[end] = array[end], array[start]\n            start += 1\n            end -= 1\n\n    def _find_max(array: List[Any], num_elements: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Finds the index of the maximum element in array[0...num_elements-1].\"\"\"\n        max_idx = 0\n        for i in range(1, num_elements):\n            if array[i] > array[max_idx]:\n                max_idx = i\n        return max_idx\n\n    for curr_size in range(n, 1, -1):\n        max_idx = _find_max(elements, curr_size)\n\n        if max_idx != curr_size - 1:\n            _flip(elements, max_idx + 1)\n            _flip(elements, curr_size)\n\n    return elements"}
