{"task_id": "Mbpp/222", "solution": "def check_type(input_tuple: tuple) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if all elements in a tuple have the same data type.\n    Returns True for empty or single-element tuples.\"\"\"\n\n    n = len(input_tuple)\n\n    # An empty tuple or a tuple with a single element is considered to have all elements of the same type.\n    if n <= 1:\n        return True\n\n    # Get the type of the first element to compare with others.\n    first_element_type = type(input_tuple[0])\n\n    # Iterate from the second element to check if all subsequent elements match the first element's type.\n    for i in range(1, n):\n        if type(input_tuple[i]) is not first_element_type:\n            return False # Found an element with a different type\n\n    return True # All elements have the same data type"}
