{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets all even-indexed bits (0, 2, 4, ...) of an integer to 1.\n    A mask is generated to set even bits up to the number's relevant bit length.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Determine the number of bits to consider for the mask, based on the absolute value.\n    max_bit_len = abs(number).bit_length()\n\n    # Create a mask with 1s at all even bit positions within the relevant range.\n    even_bits_mask = 0\n    i = 0\n    while i < max_bit_len:\n        even_bits_mask |= (1 << i)\n        i += 2\n\n    # Perform a bitwise OR operation to set all target even bits to 1.\n    return number | even_bits_mask"}
