{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "def check_occurences(input_list: list[tuple]) -> dict[tuple, int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the occurrences of canonical tuples in a list of tuples.\n    This function processes each tuple by sorting its elements to create a canonical form.\n    \"\"\"\n    occurrences_dict = {}\n    for original_tuple in input_list:\n        # Convert tuple to list, sort, then convert back to tuple for canonical form.\n        temp_list = list(original_tuple)\n        temp_list.sort()\n        canonical_tuple = tuple(temp_list)\n\n        # Increment count for the canonical tuple.\n        if canonical_tuple in occurrences_dict:\n            occurrences_dict[canonical_tuple] += 1\n        else:\n            occurrences_dict[canonical_tuple] = 1\n    return occurrences_dict"}
