{"task_id": "Mbpp/244", "solution": "def next_Perfect_Square(number: float) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the smallest perfect square strictly greater than the input number.\n    It determines the next integer whose square is above the input.\"\"\"\n\n    # Calculate the square root of the input number.\n    sqrt_val = number ** 0.5\n\n    # Determine the next integer 'k' such that k*k will be the desired perfect square.\n    # This covers both cases: if number is a perfect square (e.g., sqrt(36)=6.0, next_int=7)\n    # or if it's not (e.g., sqrt(35)=5.9..., next_int=6).\n    next_int = int(sqrt_val) + 1\n\n    # The result is the square of this next integer.\n    return next_int * next_int"}
