{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "def find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the n'th Lucas number.\n    It uses an iterative approach based on L(0)=2, L(1)=1, and L(n)=L(n-1)+L(n-2).\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n    # For n > 1, use an iterative approach to compute the Lucas number.\n    a, b = 2, 1  # L(0), L(1)\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        a, b = b, a + b\n    return b"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "def get_max_sum(n: int, _cache: dict = None) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the maximum sum for n using the recursive equation f(n) = max((f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    Memoization is used to optimize performance by storing results of previously computed sub-problems.\"\"\"\n    if _cache is None:\n        _cache = {}\n\n    if n in _cache:\n        return _cache[n]\n\n    # Base case: if n is 0 or very small, the sum of sub-problems might be 0,\n    # so max(sum_of_sub_problems, n) correctly returns n.\n    # For example, f(0) = max(f(0)+f(0)+f(0)+f(0), 0) which resolves to 0.\n    # f(1) = max(f(0)+f(0)+f(0)+f(0), 1) which resolves to 1.\n    sum_of_subproblems = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2, _cache) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 3, _cache) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 4, _cache) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 5, _cache)\n    )\n\n    result = max(sum_of_subproblems, n)\n    _cache[n] = result\n    return result"}
