{"task_id": "Mbpp/398", "solution": "def sum_of_digits(numbers_list: list) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the sum of digits for each number in a given list and returns the total sum.\n\n    Args:\n        numbers_list: A list of integers.\n\n    Returns:\n        The sum of digits of each number in the list.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    total_sum_of_all_digits = 0\n    for number in numbers_list:\n        # Calculate the sum of digits for the current number\n        current_number_digit_sum = 0\n        # Use absolute value to handle potential negative numbers gracefully\n        abs_number = abs(number)\n\n        # If the number is 0, its sum of digits is 0\n        if abs_number == 0:\n            current_number_digit_sum = 0\n        else:\n            # Iterate through digits by repeatedly taking modulo 10 and dividing by 10\n            temp_number = abs_number\n            while temp_number > 0:\n                current_number_digit_sum += temp_number % 10\n                temp_number //= 10\n\n        total_sum_of_all_digits += current_number_digit_sum\n\n    return total_sum_of_all_digits"}
