{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "def _get_perrin_number(k: int) -> int:\n    # Handle base cases for Perrin numbers P(0), P(1), P(2).\n    if k == 0:\n        return 3\n    if k == 1:\n        return 0\n    if k == 2:\n        return 2\n\n    # Initialize the first three Perrin numbers for iterative calculation.\n    # p_k_minus_3 represents P(i-3), p_k_minus_2 represents P(i-2), p_k_minus_1 represents P(i-1).\n    p_k_minus_3, p_k_minus_2, p_k_minus_1 = 3, 0, 2 # These correspond to P(0), P(1), P(2)\n\n    # Calculate Perrin numbers iteratively using the recurrence relation.\n    for _ in range(3, k + 1):\n        current_p = p_k_minus_3 + p_k_minus_2\n        p_k_minus_3 = p_k_minus_2\n        p_k_minus_2 = p_k_minus_1\n        p_k_minus_1 = current_p\n    return p_k_minus_1\ndef cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    # Return 0 if n is negative, as specified by the design.\n    if n < 0:\n        return 0\n\n    total_sum = 0\n    # Iterate from 0 to n (inclusive), summing each Perrin number.\n    for i in range(n + 1):\n        total_sum += _get_perrin_number(i)\n    return total_sum"}
