{"task_id": "Mbpp/560", "solution": "def union_elements(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the union of elements from two input tuples, ensuring uniqueness\n    and sorting them in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    combined_elements = list(tuple1) + list(tuple2)\n    unique_elements_list = list(set(combined_elements))\n    sorted_unique_elements = sorted(unique_elements_list)\n    return tuple(sorted_unique_elements)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/560", "solution": "def union_elements(tuple1: tuple, tuple2: tuple) -> tuple:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the union of elements from two given tuples and outputs them in sorted order.\n\n    Args:\n        tuple1 (tuple): The first input tuple.\n        tuple2 (tuple): The second input tuple.\n\n    Returns:\n        tuple: A new tuple containing all unique elements from both input tuples,\n               sorted in ascending order.\n\n    Example:\n        >>> union_elements((3, 4, 5, 6), (5, 7, 4, 10))\n        (3, 4, 5, 6, 7, 10)\n    \"\"\"\n    # Combine elements from both tuples\n    combined_elements = tuple1 + tuple2\n\n    # Use a set to get unique elements\n    unique_elements = set(combined_elements)\n\n    # Convert to a list and sort in ascending order\n    sorted_unique_elements_list = sorted(list(unique_elements))\n\n    # Convert the sorted list back to a tuple and return\n    return tuple(sorted_unique_elements_list)"}
