{"task_id": "Mbpp/589", "solution": "import math\ndef perfect_squares(start, end):\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies all perfect squares within a specified inclusive range [start, end].\n    Returns a list of these perfect squares in ascending order.\n    \"\"\"\n    if start > end:\n        return []\n\n    results = []\n    # Calculate the smallest integer 'i' whose square is greater than or equal to 'start'.\n    i = math.ceil(math.sqrt(max(0, start)))\n\n    while True:\n        current_square = i * i\n        if current_square > end:\n            break\n\n        # Add the perfect square to the list if it falls within the specified range.\n        results.append(current_square)\n        i += 1\n\n    return results"}
