{"task_id": "Mbpp/599", "solution": "def sum_average(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum and average of the first n natural numbers.\n    Assumes n is a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    calculated_sum = n * (n + 1) // 2\n    calculated_average = float(calculated_sum) / n\n    return (calculated_sum, calculated_average)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/597", "solution": "def find_kth(arr1: list[int], arr2: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the k-th smallest element from two combined sorted arrays.\n    Uses a binary search approach for optimal time complexity O(log(min(len(arr1), len(arr2)))).\n    \"\"\"\n    m, n = len(arr1), len(arr2)\n\n    # Ensure arr1 is the shorter array to optimize binary search range.\n    if m > n:\n        arr1, arr2 = arr2, arr1\n        m, n = n, m\n\n    # Define the search space for 'cut1', the number of elements taken from arr1.\n    # 'low' ensures enough elements are available from arr2 if k is large.\n    # 'high' ensures cut1 does not exceed arr1's length or k itself.\n    low = max(0, k - n)\n    high = min(k, m)\n\n    while low <= high:\n        cut1 = (low + high) // 2\n        cut2 = k - cut1\n\n        # Get the elements at the partition boundaries, using -infinity and +infinity for edge cases.\n        left1 = arr1[cut1 - 1] if cut1 > 0 else float('-inf')\n        right1 = arr1[cut1] if cut1 < m else float('inf')\n        left2 = arr2[cut2 - 1] if cut2 > 0 else float('-inf')\n        right2 = arr2[cut2] if cut2 < n else float('inf')\n\n        # Check if the partition is valid.\n        # This means all elements in the left partition are less than or equal to all elements in the right partition.\n        if left1 <= right2 and left2 <= right1:\n            return max(left1, left2)  # The k-th element is the maximum of the two left partition elements.\n        elif left1 > right2:\n            high = cut1 - 1  # arr1's left part is too large, need to take fewer elements from arr1.\n        else:  # left2 > right1\n            low = cut1 + 1   # arr2's left part is too large, need to take more elements from arr1.\n\n    # This return statement should ideally not be reached if inputs adhere to preconditions.\n    return -1"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/599", "solution": "def sum_average(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum and average of the first n natural numbers.\n    It assumes `n` is a positive integer, as per the critical requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = n * (n + 1) / 2\n    average = total_sum / n\n    return (total_sum, average)"}
