{"task_id": "Mbpp/605", "solution": "def prime_num(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given integer is a prime number.\n    Returns True if the number is prime, False otherwise.\"\"\"\n    if number <= 1:\n        return False\n    if number == 2:\n        return True\n    if number % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n\n    # Check for odd divisors from 3 up to the square root of number\n    # The range step is 2 to check only odd numbers.\n    for i in range(3, int(number**0.5) + 1, 2):\n        if number % i == 0:\n            return False\n\n    return True"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "def bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the Nth Bell Number.\n\n    This function computes Bell numbers using Stirling numbers of the second kind.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # stirling_numbers[i][k] stores S(i, k), Stirling number of the second kind\n    stirling_numbers = [[0 for _ in range(n + 1)] for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: S(0, 0) = 1\n    stirling_numbers[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the Stirling numbers table using the recurrence relation\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # S(i, 0) = 0 for i > 0\n        stirling_numbers[i][0] = 0\n        for k in range(1, i + 1):\n            stirling_numbers[i][k] = stirling_numbers[i-1][k-1] + k * stirling_numbers[i-1][k]\n\n    # The Nth Bell number is the sum of S(n, k) for k from 0 to n\n    bell_n = sum(stirling_numbers[n][k] for k in range(n + 1))\n\n    return bell_n"}
