{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "def bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth Bell number using a dynamic programming approach (Bell triangle).\n    Assumes input `n` is a non-negative integer.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize a 2D array (Bell triangle)\n    bell_triangle = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case for the Bell triangle\n    bell_triangle[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Populate the Bell triangle\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # First element of the current row is the last element of the previous row\n        bell_triangle[i][0] = bell_triangle[i-1][i-1]\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            # Each subsequent element is the sum of the element to its left\n            # and the element diagonally up-left from the previous row\n            bell_triangle[i][j] = bell_triangle[i][j-1] + bell_triangle[i-1][j-1]\n\n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the nth row\n    return bell_triangle[n][0]"}
