{"task_id": "Mbpp/611", "solution": "def max_of_nth(matrix: list[list[int]], n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum value in the n-th column of a matrix.\n    Raises ValueError if the matrix is empty or IndexError if n is out of bounds.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not matrix:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input matrix cannot be empty.\")\n\n    num_cols = len(matrix[0])\n    if not (0 <= n < num_cols):\n        raise IndexError(f\"Column index {n} is out of bounds for a matrix with {num_cols} columns.\")\n\n    max_val = matrix[0][n]\n    for row in matrix:\n        if row[n] > max_val:\n            max_val = row[n]\n\n    return max_val"}
