{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "solution": "def get_coordinates(coordinate_tuple: tuple[int, int]) -> list[list[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Extracts all 9 adjacent coordinates for a given 2D point, including the point itself.\n    Returns a list of lists, where each inner list represents an adjacent [x', y'] coordinate.\n    \"\"\"\n    x, y = coordinate_tuple\n    adjacent_coords = []\n\n    for dx in range(-1, 2):  # Iterate through relative x-offsets: -1, 0, 1\n        for dy in range(-1, 2):  # Iterate through relative y-offsets: -1, 0, 1\n            new_x = x + dx\n            new_y = y + dy\n            adjacent_coords.append([new_x, new_y])\n\n    return adjacent_coords"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/630", "solution": "def get_coordinates(coordinate):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates all coordinates in a 3x3 grid centered at the input coordinate (x, y).\n    Returns a list of lists, where each inner list represents an adjacent coordinate [x', y'].\n    \"\"\"\n    x, y = coordinate\n    adjacent_coords = []\n\n    for x_prime in range(x - 1, x + 2):\n        for y_prime in range(y - 1, y + 2):\n            adjacent_coords.append([x_prime, y_prime])\n\n    return adjacent_coords"}
