{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def heap_sort(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of numbers in-place using the heap sort algorithm.\n    It first builds a max-heap, then repeatedly extracts the largest element.\"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n\n    _build_max_heap(input_list)\n\n    # One by one extract elements from heap\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        input_list[i], input_list[0] = input_list[0], input_list[i]  # Swap root with last element\n        _heapify(input_list, i, 0)  # Call _heapify on the reduced heap\n\n    return input_list"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/635", "solution": "def heap_sort(input_list: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Sorts a list of elements in ascending order using the heap sort algorithm.\n    This function modifies the input list in-place and returns it.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n\n    # Build a max-heap from the list by heapifying all non-leaf subtrees\n    for i in range(n // 2 - 1, -1, -1):\n        _heapify(input_list, n, i)\n\n    # Extract elements one by one from the heap and place them at the end of the list\n    for i in range(n - 1, 0, -1):\n        input_list[i], input_list[0] = input_list[0], input_list[i]  # Swap root with current last element\n        _heapify(input_list, i, 0)  # Restore max-heap property on the reduced heap\n\n    return input_list"}
