{"task_id": "Mbpp/644", "solution": "def reverse_Array_Upto_K(arr: list, k: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Reverses elements of an array from the beginning up to a specified 1-based position K.\n    Returns a new list with the modified elements, leaving subsequent elements unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    if k < 1:\n        return list(arr) # Return a copy of the original list if k is invalid.\n\n    # Slice the array from the beginning up to K (exclusive for k in 0-based indexing)\n    # The slice arr[0:k] will correctly handle cases where k >= len(arr) by taking the whole array.\n    portion_to_reverse = arr[0:k]\n    reversed_portion = portion_to_reverse[::-1]\n\n    # Get the remaining part of the array, which should not be reversed\n    remaining_portion = arr[k:]\n\n    # Concatenate the reversed portion with the untouched remaining portion\n    return reversed_portion + remaining_portion"}
