{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "def maxAverageOfPath(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum average cost of a path from (0,0) to (N-1, N-1)\n    in a square matrix using dynamic programming.\n    \"\"\"\n    N = len(matrix)\n\n    # Initialize DP table with floats to store maximum total costs.\n    dp = [[0.0] * N for _ in range(N)]\n\n    # Base case: The cost to reach (0,0) is its own value.\n    dp[0][0] = float(matrix[0][0])\n\n    # Fill the first row: Only movement to the right is possible.\n    for c in range(1, N):\n        dp[0][c] = float(matrix[0][c]) + dp[0][c-1]\n\n    # Fill the first column: Only movement downwards is possible.\n    for r in range(1, N):\n        dp[r][0] = float(matrix[r][0]) + dp[r-1][0]\n\n    # Fill the remaining DP table cells based on paths from above or left.\n    for r in range(1, N):\n        for c in range(1, N):\n            dp[r][c] = float(matrix[r][c]) + max(dp[r-1][c], dp[r][c-1])\n\n    # Retrieve the maximum total cost to the bottom-right cell.\n    max_total_cost = dp[N-1][N-1]\n\n    # The number of cells in any valid path is fixed.\n    num_cells = 2 * N - 1\n\n    # Calculate and return the maximum average cost.\n    max_average_cost = max_total_cost / num_cells\n\n    return max_average_cost"}
