{"task_id": "Mbpp/721", "solution": "def maxAverageOfPath(matrix: list[list[int]]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum average cost of a path from the top-left to the bottom-right cell\n    in a square matrix, moving only right or down.\n\n    Args:\n        matrix: A square matrix given as a list of lists of integers, where each cell\n                is associated with a specific cost.\n\n    Returns:\n        The maximum average over all existing paths. Average is computed as total cost\n        divided by the number of cells visited in the path.\n    \"\"\"\n    N = len(matrix)\n\n    # Handle the case of an empty matrix or invalid N (though problem implies N >= 1)\n    if N == 0:\n        return 0.0\n    if N == 1:\n        return float(matrix[0][0])\n\n    # Initialize DP table\n    dp_table = [[0.0 for _ in range(N)] for _ in range(N)]\n\n    # Base case: The cost to reach the top-left cell is its own value.\n    dp_table[0][0] = float(matrix[0][0])\n\n    # Populate the first row (can only come from the left)\n    for j in range(1, N):\n        dp_table[0][j] = float(matrix[0][j]) + dp_table[0][j-1]\n\n    # Populate the first column (can only come from above)\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        dp_table[i][0] = float(matrix[i][0]) + dp_table[i-1][0]\n\n    # Populate the rest of the DP table\n    for i in range(1, N):\n        for j in range(1, N):\n            dp_table[i][j] = float(matrix[i][j]) + max(dp_table[i-1][j], dp_table[i][j-1])\n\n    # The maximum total cost will be in the bottom-right cell of the DP table.\n    max_total_cost = dp_table[N-1][N-1]\n\n    # The number of cells visited in any path from top-left to bottom-right is constant.\n    path_length = 2 * N - 1\n\n    # Calculate and return the maximum average.\n    return max_total_cost / path_length"}
