{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list: list, count: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Rotates the input_list to the right by count positions.\n    Returns a new list with the items rotated circularly to the right.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n\n    if n == 0 or count == 0:\n        return input_list[:]\n\n    effective_count = count % n\n    if effective_count == 0:  # If effective_count is 0 after modulo, no rotation is needed\n        return input_list[:]\n\n    split_point = n - effective_count\n    tail_part = input_list[split_point:]\n    head_part = input_list[:split_point]\n\n    return tail_part + head_part"}
