{"task_id": "Mbpp/743", "solution": "def rotate_right(input_list: list, rotation_count: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Rotates a list to the right by a specified number of items.\n    Returns a new list with elements reordered, leaving the original list unchanged.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(input_list)\n    if n == 0:\n        return []\n\n    effective_rotation_count = rotation_count % n\n\n    # Split the list into two parts: suffix (elements to move to the front)\n    # and prefix (the remaining elements that follow the suffix).\n    suffix = input_list[n - effective_rotation_count:]\n    prefix = input_list[:n - effective_rotation_count]\n\n    return suffix + prefix"}
