{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "def _has_zero_digit(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given number contains the digit '0'.\"\"\"\n    return '0' in str(number)\ndef _is_divisible_by_all_non_zero_digits(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Determines if a number is evenly divisible by all its non-zero constituent digits.\"\"\"\n    for digit_char in str(number):\n        digit = int(digit_char)\n        # The design specification ensures numbers with '0' are filtered out by _has_zero_digit\n        # But this function specifically checks non-zero digits, so we guard against 0 here too\n        if digit != 0:\n            if number % digit != 0:\n                return False\n    return True\ndef divisible_by_digits(startnum: int, endnum: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds numbers within a range that are divisible by all their non-zero constituent digits.\n    It iterates through the range, delegating checks to helper functions.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_list = []\n    for n in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        if not _has_zero_digit(n):\n            if _is_divisible_by_all_non_zero_digits(n):\n                result_list.append(n)\n    return result_list"}
