{"task_id": "Mbpp/786", "solution": "def right_insertion(list: list, value: object) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Locates the right insertion point for a value in a sorted list using binary search.\n    It returns an index `i` such that all elements `e` in `list[0:i]` satisfy `e <= value`,\n    and all elements `e` in `list[i:]` satisfy `e > value`.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(list)\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if list[mid] <= value:\n            # The insertion point is at or after mid + 1.\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:  # list[mid] > value\n            # The insertion point is at or before mid.\n            high = mid\n    return low"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/778", "solution": "def pack_consecutive_duplicates(input_list: list) -> list[list]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Packs consecutive duplicate elements of a given list into sublists.\n    It groups identical, adjacent elements while preserving their original order.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    packed_list = []\n    current_sublist = [input_list[0]]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(input_list)):\n        if input_list[i] == current_sublist[0]:\n            current_sublist.append(input_list[i])\n        else:\n            packed_list.append(current_sublist)\n            current_sublist = [input_list[i]]\n\n    packed_list.append(current_sublist)\n\n    return packed_list"}
